> Stupid Ascension Trick 3.4.5, only beach-wear
>
> I had done a version of this in 2005, but it was a relaxed
> one where I allowed myself to wear armor up to the Castle.
> This one is a strict beach-wear. Nothing other than
> Hawaiian shirts were ever worn. (I did finish with my
> original shirt, but I briefly wore another one I found before
> evaporating it trying to get a +6 shirt.)
>
> I found this to be a bit difficult. I lost quite a few games
> in the early stages, trying to run the protection racket. The
> most frequent cause was getting separated from my pets, or
> meeting a gnome with a wand.
>
> This particular game started with one blessed potion of extra
> healing, so the boost from 10 HP to 15 HP definitely helped.
> After the initial protection, it went pretty smoothly. I spent
> some time with teleportitis, but I've done that before.
>
> Sacrafices gave Vorpy, which I used a small amount, then
> Magicbane which I wielded for the rest of the game, #twoweaponing
> with a long sword later on.
>
> Wishes went for scrolls of charging (just in case the wand was
> 0:1, but I could have save that wish and just used the PYEC a bit
> later), Eyes of the Overworld (because lenses are allowed, and
> Astral vision is very cool), spellbook of identify, a bag of
> holding (because I didn't find one until very late, and I wanted
> to carry more than an unburdened amount of stuff), and a ring
> of levitation (because I never found or produced one, and did
> not want to deal with the Plane of Air without one). I finished
> with an unused regular wish and a wrestable one.
>
> The PYEC does make it easy to rely on wand charges. I spent
> teleportation and death zaps freely. I finished with 10 death
> zaps ready in my main inventory, and I think at least another
> 20 in my bag.
>
> With only -4 AC, I was getting beat on pretty heavily on the
> Astral Plane. My 300 HP and teleportation zaps made it possible
> to get to Famine's side, which was the correct one, so I finished
> pretty easily. If I would have had to go back to another one, I
> probably would have had to use some conflict, maybe scrolls of
> scare monster, regeneration.
>
> I only jotted down a few notes. After the Castle, there was
> not anything very interesting (compared to other ascensions).
>
> Not that these are any great insights, but these attempts pointed
> out that the big dangers for me are very low hit points at the
> begining (when attempting a protection racket), and feeling
> overconfident at around experience level 9 or 10. Once I have
> reflection, magic resistance (especially from Magicbane), and
> a moderate weapon, the rest is pretty easy.
>
